s Pete Thamel on Monday night.","published":"2026-11-17T02:45:08.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50506952/sources-butch-jones-arkansas-state-coach","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Top 25 betting lines: UGA big faves over Gamecocks, Vols slim favorites vs. LSU","description":"This week's odds and FPI predictions for South Carolina-Georgia, Tennessee-LSU and more.","published":"2026-11-16T23:15:08.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/espn/betting/story/_/id/50498153/2026-college-football-week-12-top-25-betting-lines-odds","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Illinois may turn to third-string QB Boyd after Houser injury","description":"Illinois might turn to third-string quarterback Carson Boyd this week against No. 15 Iowa after starter Katin Houser suffered a broken nose Friday at UCLA that required surgery.","published":"2026-11-16T21:42:38.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50504718/illinois-turn-third-string-qb-boyd-houser-injury","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Rivers says NC State only college job he would have taken","description":"New coach Philip Rivers said NC State was the only college job he would have taken.","published":"2026-11-17T12:34:08.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50504530/rivers-says-nc-state-only-college-job-taken","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"David Hale","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Wake Forest up to No. 10 in AP poll as top teams avoid upsets","description":"Wake Forest's move up to No. 10 was the only week-over-week change atop the AP poll as the top nine teams remained unchanged.","published":"2026-11-16T20:48:17.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50504044/wake-forest-no-10-ap-poll-top-teams-avoid-upsets","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Texas' Manning to participate in senior day, mum on future","description":"Texas quarterback Arch Manning said Monday he will participate in Saturday's senior day ceremonies despite having one year of eligibility remaining.","published":"2026-11-16T20:31:37.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50503997/texas-arch-manning-participate-senior-day","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5082149/clev-lubin","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clev_Lubin"},"pick":{"pick":57,"round":2,"team":"KC","provisional":true},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Clev Lubin","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clev_Lubin","description":"American football player","touched":"2026-11-14T07:37:13Z","intro":"Clevmer Lubin (CLEV-mah LOO-bin) is an American college football defensive end for the Louisville Cardinals. He previously played for the Army Black Knights, Iowa Western Reivers, and Coastal Carolina Chanticleers.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Lubin played football and basketball for Suffern High School and was considered one of the best players the school has produced. He played as both a defensive end and running back, and during his senior season he recorded 1,053 rushing yards and 16 touchdowns on 110 carries. He also set a program record of 1,062 rushing yards during the 2019 season. Due to his success on the field, he was named the Gatorade New York State Player of the Year as a senior and was also named The Journal News Rockland County Football Player of the Year. Lubin received several Division I offers, and on December 14, 2020, he committed to play at Army. Following his senior season, Lubin spent a year prepping at USMAPS before joining the Black Knights in 2022."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"ARMY\nAfter joining the Black Knights, Lubin did not see any game action his true freshman season and transferred to Iowa Western.\n\nIOWA WESTERN\nWhile at Iowa Western, Lubin helped lead the team to the NJCAA D1 Football National Championship. Following the season he was named a first-team NJCAA All-American.\n\nCOASTAL CAROLINA\nOn July 1, 2024, Lubin enrolled at Coastal Carolina. In 10 games, he finished 16th nationally in sacks and contributed 12.5 tackles for loss. Following the season, he was given First-Team All-Sun Belt honors.\nAfter the season, Lubin again entered the transfer portal.\n\nLOUISVILLE\nOn December 21, 2024, Lubin committed to Louisville. On January 2, 2026, Lubin announced he would return to Louisville for another season."}]}}